 ## Rollout and rollback consequences
 
-- Production uses one model proposal followed by deterministic admission; a second model may score sealed replay or Shadow artifacts but has no write authority.
+- Production presents one authoritative composite semantic proposal to
+  deterministic Admission.  Since the 2026-07-19 ADR 0024 amendment, that
+  composite may contain a bounded structural clause recovery described below;
+  an independent second model vote may score sealed replay or Shadow artifacts
+  but has no write authority.
+
+## 2026-07-19 bounded structural recovery amendment
+
+The original one-proposal rule prohibited competing model votes and alternate
+write routers.  It did not account for a primary model segment that spans
+several explicitly separated source clauses and erases a sibling business
+goal.  ADR 0024 now permits the Semantic Interpreter to build its one
+authoritative composite proposal from:
+
+1. one normal primary semantic proposal; and
+2. at most one non-recursive, single-attempt semantic proposal for each of 2-6
+   explicitly punctuation-separated clauses when structural coverage is
+   missing or a primary action segment crosses clause boundaries.
+
+Clause recovery uses the same closed cognition contract and permission-scoped
+resources.  It cannot call Planner/Executor, select database IDs, vote on
+write success, retry its schema/transport call, invoke another focused
+recovery, or bypass Admission.  Source offsets, action multiplicity and
+original action anchors must all be preserved.  If any broad-segment clause
+fails or preservation cannot be proved, the composite becomes a deterministic
+zero-action clarification; the broad proposal is not admitted.  Recovery
+policy parameters are part of Runtime identity and all recovered fragments are
+namespaced into the original source coordinate system.
 - New controls default off, run in Shadow first, and remain fenced to the existing Sandbox tenant and the Pang Hao/Liu Cong Canary allowlist.
 - Turning Admission off never means allow-all. Rollback must first route to a known-good runtime or block writes, revoke/expire outstanding Tickets, and preserve audit evidence.
 - Source spans, Ticket claims, receipt linkage, and PostgreSQL round trips are deterministic test surfaces.
